    {
      "id": "870bad13-6d04-4550-a773-027d613675d5",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-23T19:58:46.000Z",
      "title": "New major risk - Revenue and earnings growth",
      "body": "Earnings are forecast to decline by an average of 1.2% per year for the foreseeable future. This is considered a major risk. Ultimately, shareholders want to see a good return on their investment and that generally comes from sharing in the company's profits. If profits are expected to decline, then in most cases the share price will decline over time as well. In addition, if the company pays dividends it will also likely need to reduce or cut them, striking a dual blow to total shareholder returns. Currently, the following risks have been identified for the company: Major Risks Earnings are forecast to decline by an average of 1.2% per year for the foreseeable future. High level of non-cash earnings (113% accrual ratio). Minor Risk Paying a dividend despite having no free cash flows.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c6dfa73-1904-48cd-a1ce-bc3d309f1d7e",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-23T19:58:45.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues exceed analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹90.84 (up from ₹80.89 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹9.81t (up 10% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹644.3b (up 26% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 6.6% (up from 5.7% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 2.7%. Earnings per share (EPS) also surpassed analyst estimates by 13%. Revenue is forecast to grow 5.7% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 11% growth forecast for the Insurance industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 8% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 10% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
